  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 306 PM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nThe extended forecast begins with decreasing coverage of showers and \nthunderstorms as a cold front pushes the slow-moving surface low out \nof the region, bringing an end to the prolonged period of heavy \nrainfall that has affected the area since Tuesday. Behind the front, \ncold air advection will support cooler, much more autumn-like \ntemperatures starting Friday and persisting through much of the \nextended period. In addition to the cooler temperatures, surface \nhigh pressure will build across the region, keeping conditions \npredominantly dry. However, long-term deterministic models indicate \na minor shortwave passing through the area Saturday night into \nSunday, though measurable precipitation associated with this feature \nwill likely be confined to northern portions of the CWA. Otherwise, \nsurface high pressure rapidly reestablishes itself, ensuring a \ncontinued period of seasonable autumn weather across the region.\n\nA passing cold front will clear the slow-moving surface low out of \nthe region, putting an end to the persistent heavy rainfall seen \nsince Tuesday. High pressure and post-frontal cold air advection \nwill bring cooler, dry, autumn-like conditions from Friday through \nthe extended forecast period, with only a minor shortwave bringing a \nbrief chance of precipitation to northern portions of the area over \nthe weekend.",
